## Exp52 — Causal Intraday Regime Timing Family — FAIL

Purpose: test a genuinely new causal day/session context family for binary EXIT-vs-NO_EXIT, using only information available at state_time. Frozen features were TOD_SIN/TOD_COS, LOG_DAY_RANGE_ATR, LOG_DAY_PATH_ATR, DAY_EFFICIENCY. Same 24 elapsed-step intercepts; TRAIN-only fits; same exact 8 direction×time environments; same H={15,30,60,120}; primary JOINT5_EXIT vs BASE_EXIT on EXIT_STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED with whole-BRT-day bootstrap.

Implementation note before score: initial runner aborted at the state_time feature join because dyn can contain multiple corridor states at one timestamp while the M5 feature map is unique by timestamp. This was corrected from one_to_one to many_to_one with explicit cardinality-preservation guards. No score had been accepted before the correction and no scientific rule changed.

All environment scorability guards PASS. TRAIN feature rank=5/5; standardized condition number=7.739603; JOINT5 design rank=29/29; convergence=True; finite=True. EXP52_JOINT5_IDENTIFIABILITY=PASS.

Formal JOINT5 vs BASE:
VAL_EARLY_UP Brier -.000476069 CI[-.005049888,+.004799074] FAIL; LL -.000932630 CI[-.011066765,+.010929457] FAIL.
VAL_EARLY_DOWN +.004182493 CI[-.002984698,+.011542882] FAIL; LL +.009471187 CI[-.006501926,+.025794464] FAIL.
VAL_LATE_UP +.001564937 CI[-.003660861,+.007320395] FAIL; LL +.003345191 CI[-.008188284,+.016543114] FAIL.
VAL_LATE_DOWN -.000919168 CI[-.004513160,+.004811811] FAIL; LL -.002040329 CI[-.010084550,+.010898165] FAIL.
