TEST_LATE_UP -.002199739 CI[-.005389639,+.001841575] FAIL; LL -.004577717 CI[-.011443634,+.004533998] FAIL.
TEST_LATE_DOWN -.001255502 CI[-.006960405,+.006098551] FAIL; LL -.002822838 CI[-.015623693,+.013014013] FAIL.

Formal cells passing: 0/16. Therefore EXP52_EXIT_ENVIRONMENT_STATUS=PASS; EXP52_JOINT5_IDENTIFIABILITY=PASS; INTRADAY_REGIME_TIMING_FAMILY=FAIL; ROBUST_INTRADAY_EXIT_CLOCK_CONTEXT=FAIL; EXP52_FORMAL_STATUS=FAIL.

Diagnostics reinforced the failure: AUC direction itself inverted across environments, e.g. TEST_EARLY_UP approximately 0.22–0.35 and VALIDATION_LATE_DOWN approximately 0.39–0.47, while some DOWN environments were above 0.5. Therefore failure is not only calibration. Marginal/drop-one diagnostics cannot rescue.

Interpretation: cumulative day/session context as defined here is not a universal historical EXIT clock. Exp47 remains the minimal robust historical probability law: elapsed-time BASE clock plus Position for conditional side.

## Exp53 — Nearest-Edge M5 Impulse Timing Family — FROZEN BEFORE SCORE

This is the FINAL preregistered historical timing-feature family before the fresh-forward gate. If Exp53 fails or is underpowered, HISTORICAL_TIMING_FEATURE_DISCOVERY_STOP=YES and no Exp54 historical timing-feature search is allowed.

Scientific question: does the local closed-M5 impulse at state_time, oriented toward the nearest fixed corridor boundary, add a robust EXIT-vs-NO_EXIT clock component beyond BASE_EXIT?

Frozen causal features, all computed from the single M5 bar closed at state_time and current frozen corridor:
- nearest boundary = BACK when |close-back| <= |forward-close|, otherwise FORWARD; this tie rule is frozen.
- EDGE_BODY_ATR = edge_sign * (M5_close - M5_open) / ATR. Positive means net candle body toward nearest edge.
- BAR_RANGE_ATR = (M5_high - M5_low) / ATR. Unsigned local M5 range.
- EDGE_CLOSE_LOC = edge_sign * (2*M5_close - M5_high - M5_low)/(M5_high-M5_low), clipped to [-1,1], and defined 0 for zero-range bars. Positive means close pressure toward nearest edge.

Excluded from Exp53: static distance magnitude, Position as timing predictor, Dwell, day/session context, lookback-window search, multiple window lengths, interactions, thresholds, feature subsets chosen after score, OOS refit or recalibration.

Models, TRAIN only, same 24 frozen elapsed-step intercepts:
BASE_EXIT = frozen intercepts only.
BODY_EXIT = BASE + EDGE_BODY_ATR.
RANGE_EXIT = BASE + BAR_RANGE_ATR.
PRESSURE_EXIT = BASE + EDGE_CLOSE_LOC.
JOINT3_EXIT = BASE + all three frozen features.
DROP_BODY / DROP_RANGE / DROP_PRESSURE are diagnostic only.

Required analysis: exact EXP52 replay must preserve FAIL before any Exp53 score; causal state-time/OHLC mapping guards; TRAIN-only correlation/rank; JOINT3 identifiability; marginal Holm diagnostics across 3×8×2=48 tests; horizon point gains; drop-one; AUC/calibration; primary whole-BRT-day bootstrap.

Primary formal comparison: JOINT3_EXIT vs exact BASE_EXIT using binary Brier and LogLoss on EXIT_STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED cells within the exact eight direction×time environments. Formal PASS requires CI95 lower bound >0 for both metrics in all 8 environments = 16/16.

LOCAL_EDGE_IMPULSE_TIMING_FAMILY=PASS only at 16/16. ROBUST_LOCAL_EDGE_EXIT_IMPULSE=PASS only with all environments scorable, JOINT3 numerically identifiable, and 16/16 formal cells.

Frozen stop rule: if Exp53 is FAIL or UNDERPOWERED, HISTORICAL_TIMING_FEATURE_DISCOVERY_STOP=YES. Preserve Exp47 baseline timing law and wait for fresh-forward Exp27 before any further timing-family claim. No historical rescue experiment may replace this stop rule.

Anti-rescue: no alternate nearest-edge rule; no candle transform; no added feature; no subset; no horizon/environment drop; no pooled-horizon replacement; no side/era-specific fit; no recalibration/intercept/threshold; no Validation/TEST refit; no Exp27 scoring/modification.

Historical OOS remains exploratory. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.
